@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Bảo Minh, "Quy tắc bảo hiểm mọi rủi ro lắp đặt": erection (installation) all risks rules.
-- THE NOUNS: DECLARE and nothing else. Every rule module imports this one.
--
-- Source: ../../source/raw/baominh-ear.txt, the `pdftotext -layout` rendering of the
-- 6-page PDF retrieved 2026-10-06 from baominh.com.vn (PDF sha256 ae94994e...5d163a).
-- A `src:N` comment quotes line N of that rendering, generated by `tools/vnsrc.py quote`;
-- no Vietnamese in a `src:` line is typed by hand.
--
-- Money is Vietnamese dong (VND), a bare NUMBER. The document prints no money figure at
-- all: every sum insured, limit and deductible is in the schedule, which is not part of
-- the document, so every one of them is an input here.
--
-- Membership test for this module: a witness of ordinary competence could testify to the
-- fact, or the schedule, the questionnaire or a claim file records it. Whether the fact
-- makes Bao Minh liable is a rule, and belongs in the module that says so. The last two
-- sections declare the vocabulary of the ANSWERS (the grounds of non-liability) and of the
-- regulative rules (parties and acts); they are enumerations, not facts.

§ `Nouns for the Bao Minh erection all risks rules`

§§ `The parties`

-- The policy speaks of two parties only: the Insured named in the schedule, and Bao Minh.
-- It never uses the Law's "purchaser of insurance"; NOTES.md section 3, fork F01.
-- (quoted at the preamble, bm-ear-general-conditions.l4: src:5-8; the short name "Bảo Minh" is defined at src:6)
DECLARE `A party to the policy` IS ONE OF
    `the Insured`
    `Bao Minh`

§§ `What caused the occurrence`

-- Every cause the document names, grouped by the clause that names it, plus one for a
-- cause it does not name. An occurrence carries a LIST of causes, because the general
-- exclusions reach a loss caused "directly or indirectly" by a named risk, and one
-- occurrence can have several causes. The list holds the causes the finder of fact held
-- operative; the rules do not weigh them (fork F17).
--
-- General exclusion (a). Each peril the list names is its own cause. Two words for a
-- strike ("đình công", "bãi công") are one cause here; see GLOSSARY.md.
-- (quoted at the rule that reads it: src:21-26)
-- General exclusion (b).
-- (quoted at the rule that reads it: src:28)
-- General exclusion (c). "representative" is not defined (Finding 12).
-- (quoted at the rule that reads it: src:30)
-- General exclusion (d).
-- (quoted at the rule that reads it: src:32)
-- Part I exclusion 3 (with its carve-back for a fault in erection) and exclusion 4.
-- (quoted at the rule that reads it: src:181-182, 184)
-- Part II exclusion 3(c).
-- (quoted at the rule that reads it: src:292-293)
-- General Condition 5(e) speaks of a loss by theft.
-- (quoted at the rule that reads it: src:105)
DECLARE `A cause of loss` IS ONE OF
    -- general exclusion (a)
    `war`
    `invasion`
    `an act of a foreign enemy`
    `hostilities, whether war is declared or not`
    `civil war`
    `riot`
    `revolution`
    `insurrection`
    `mutiny`
    `rebellion`
    `strike`
    `lockout`
    `civil commotion`
    `military action or usurped power`
    `an act of a hostile person or group acting for or in connection with a political organisation`
    `confiscation, commandeering or destruction by order of a government, de jure or de facto, or of any public authority`
    -- general exclusion (b)
    `nuclear reaction`
    `nuclear radiation`
    `radioactive contamination`
    -- general exclusion (c)
    `a wilful act of the Insured or its representative`
    `wilful negligence of the Insured or its representative`
    -- general exclusion (d)
    `cessation of work, whole or partial`
    -- Part I exclusion 3
    `faulty design`
    `defective material`
    `a defective casting or mould`
    `bad workmanship other than a fault in erection`
    `a fault in erection`
    -- Part I exclusion 4
    `corrosion`
    `wear`
    `oxidation`
    `scaling`
    -- Part II exclusion 3(c)
    `a motor vehicle licensed for use on public roads`
    `a waterborne vessel or barge`
    `an aircraft`
    -- General Condition 5(e)
    `theft`
    -- none of the above
    `a cause the policy does not name`

§§ `The kind of property lost or damaged`

-- Part I exclusion 5 lists kinds of property; Article 4 excludes construction and erection
-- plant from the surrounding-property extension.
-- (quoted at the rule that reads it: src:186-187, 241-242)
DECLARE `A kind of property` IS ONE OF
    `files`
    `drawings`
    `accounts`
    `bills`
    `currency`
    `stamps`
    `deeds`
    `evidences of debt`
    `share certificates`
    `cheques`
    `packaging materials such as cases, crates and boxes`
    `construction or erection plant, machinery or equipment`
    `property of another kind`

§§ `The works, and the items named in Part I of the schedule`

-- The works ("công trình") as a whole. Each date is NOTHING where the event has not
-- happened. These are the dates the period of insurance turns on.
-- (quoted at the rule that reads it: src:42-46)
DECLARE `The works` HAS
    `date the works commenced`                                       IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date testing began`                                             IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date the first test operation or test loading was completed`    IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date the works were handed over`                                IS A MAYBE DATE

-- One item named in Part I of the schedule ("hạng mục có tên trong Phụ lục"). The schedule
-- is not part of the document, so the number, the description and the sum insured are
-- whatever the schedule says.
-- * `sum insured`: the figure as RECORDED by Bao Minh at the time of the loss; Article 1
--   says an increase or decrease takes effect only once Bao Minh has recorded it.
-- * `full value`: for items 1 and 2, the full value of the item at the completion of
--   erection, including freight, customs duties, other taxes and erection costs (Article 1);
--   for item 4, the value of the surrounding property (Article 4, fork F23). For any other
--   item the document does not say what the full value is, and no rule reads this field
--   for it (Finding 8).
-- * the item's own dates (unloading, testing, first operation, handover) drive the partial
--   termination of cover and the second-hand rule; NOTHING where it has not happened.
-- (quoted at the rule that reads it: src:193-196, 46-47, 50-51, 53-54)
DECLARE `An item in Part I of the schedule` HAS
    `number`                          IS A NUMBER
    `description`                     IS A STRING
    `sum insured`                     IS A NUMBER
    `full value`                      IS A NUMBER
    `second-hand`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `date unloaded at the site`       IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date its testing began`          IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date its test run was completed` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date it was first operated`      IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date it was handed over`         IS A MAYBE DATE

§§ `The schedule`

-- "Phụ lục": the attached schedule. Every figure in it is an input with no default.
-- * `the Part I limit of indemnity for any one occurrence` is MAYBE: the insuring clause
--   speaks of "that limit of indemnity" without saying where it is stated (fork F14).
-- * `the sum stated separately for clearance of debris` is MAYBE: debris is covered only
--   if such a sum is stated (src:168-170).
-- * the two deductibles carry the document's two different words, "mức khấu trừ" in Part I
--   and "mức miễn thường" in Part II (GLOSSARY.md; Finding 12).
-- (quoted at the rule that reads it: src:161-163, 176, 272, 56)
DECLARE `The schedule` HAS
    `the items in Part I`                                   IS A LIST OF `An item in Part I of the schedule`
    `the total sum insured under Part I`                    IS A NUMBER
    `the Part I limit of indemnity for any one occurrence`  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the Part I deductible for each occurrence`             IS A NUMBER
    `the sum stated separately for clearance of debris`     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the Part II limit of indemnity for any one occurrence` IS A NUMBER
    `the Part II deductible for each occurrence`            IS A NUMBER
    `the date on which cover ends`                          IS A DATE

§§ `The questionnaire and the proposal form`

-- The policy is issued on the basis of the proposal form, completed by answering the
-- questionnaire ("Bản câu hỏi"), and both are part of the policy. What the questions were is
-- not in the document. The record carries only what General Condition 1 can turn on.
-- Nothing here records whether a wrong answer was material, intentional or connected with
-- the loss, because the policy asks none of those questions (Finding 2).
-- (quoted at the rule that reads it: src:5-8, 62-65)
DECLARE `The answers in the questionnaire and the proposal form` IS ONE OF
    `not given`
    `given, and every answer true and complete`
    `given, and at least one answer untrue or incomplete`

§§ `The policy`

-- * `the premium stated in the schedule has been paid`: the preamble confirms the policy
--   "on condition that" the Insured pays it; the document gives no date for payment, so
--   this records whether it had been paid when the occurrence happened (fork F05).
-- * `an extension agreed in advance in writing by Bao Minh, to`: an extension of the
--   period needs Bao Minh's prior written consent (src:56-57). NOTHING: none agreed.
-- * `a testing period agreed in writing in place of four weeks, in days`: the four weeks
--   apply "unless otherwise agreed in writing" (src:45-46). NOTHING: none agreed.
-- * `extra charges under Article 3 agreed specially in writing in advance` (src:233-235).
-- (quoted at the rule that reads it: src:10-13, 233-235)
DECLARE `The policy` HAS
    `the schedule`                                                        IS A `The schedule`
    `the works`                                                           IS A `The works`
    `the answers in the questionnaire and the proposal form`              IS A `The answers in the questionnaire and the proposal form`
    `the premium stated in the schedule has been paid`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `an extension agreed in advance in writing by Bao Minh, to`           IS A MAYBE DATE
    `a testing period agreed in writing in place of four weeks, in days`  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `extra charges under Article 3 agreed specially in writing in advance` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `What the Insured must do: the duties`

-- Each duty the document puts on the Insured, labelled with its clause. A claim records
-- the duties the Insured did NOT comply with; General Condition 1 makes compliance with
-- every one of them a condition precedent to Bao Minh's liability.
--
-- The last-but-two is not stated as a duty in so many words: General Condition 5 says
-- Bao Minh's representative "will be present to inspect" before repair, which implies the
-- Insured must not repair first (fork F11). Article 1's undertaking to adjust the sum
-- insured is in the list because it is something the Insured "undertakes" to do (Finding 4).
-- (quoted at the rule that reads it: src:73-75, 77-89, 91-105, 113-117, 122-125, 196-198, 301-308)
DECLARE `A duty of the Insured` IS ONE OF
    `GC3: take all reasonable precautions to prevent loss or liability`
    `GC3: comply with Bao Minh's reasonable recommendations`
    `GC3: comply with the manufacturer's rules and recommendations`
    `GC4(a): give Bao Minh's representative the particulars and information needed to assess the risk`
    `GC4(b): notify Bao Minh immediately, by telegram and in writing, of a material change`
    `GC4(b): take the additional precautions the circumstances require`
    `GC4(b): not make or admit, without Bao Minh's written approval, a material change increasing the risk`
    `GC5(a): notify Bao Minh immediately, by telephone or telegram and in writing, of the nature and extent of the loss`
    `GC5(b): take all steps within its power to minimise the loss`
    `GC5(c): preserve the damaged parts and make them available for inspection`
    `GC5(d): furnish the information and documents Bao Minh requires`
    `GC5(e): inform the police of a loss by theft`
    `GC5: not repair or replace, other than minor damage, before Bao Minh has inspected or a reasonable time has passed`
    `GC6: do and permit what Bao Minh requires to enforce rights against third parties`
    `Article 1: increase or decrease the sum insured when materials, wages or prices fluctuate`
    `Part II condition 1: make no admission, offer, promise, payment or indemnity without Bao Minh's written consent`
    `Part II condition 1: give Bao Minh the information and assistance it requires`

-- The Insured's conduct, as the claim file records it.
-- * The three fraud facts are about ANY claim under the policy, because General Condition 8
--   forfeits "all the benefits under this policy" (src:146), not only the claim in hand.
-- (quoted at the rule that reads it: src:141-146)
DECLARE `The conduct of the Insured` HAS
    `the duties not complied with`                                              IS A LIST OF `A duty of the Insured`
    `a claim under the policy was fraudulent`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `a false declaration was made or used in support of a claim`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `fraudulent means or devices were used to obtain a benefit under the policy` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `The occurrence`

-- "sự cố": the occurrence. It is never defined (Finding 12); the deductibles, the Part I
-- per-occurrence limit and Part II condition 2 all count by it.
-- * `on or near the site`: Part II requires the occurrence to happen on the site or in its
--   immediate vicinity (src:255-256).
-- * the two connection facts: Article 4 asks for a direct connection with ERECTION OR
--   TESTING (src:239-240); Part II asks for one with CONSTRUCTION, ERECTION OR TESTING
--   (src:255). They are kept apart because the two clauses differ (Finding 10).
-- (quoted at the rule that reads it: src:237-240, 255-256)
DECLARE `An occurrence` HAS
    `date`                                                                    IS A DATE
    `causes`                                                                  IS A LIST OF `A cause of loss`
    `on or near the site`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `directly connected with the erection or testing of the items insured under Part I` IS A BOOLEAN
    `directly connected with the construction of the items insured under Part I`        IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `A loss under Part I`

-- What was lost or damaged: part of an item named in the schedule, or surrounding property
-- of the principal or a contractor (Article 4), whose value Article 4 requires to be stated
-- at Part I item 4 of the schedule.
-- (quoted at the rule that reads it: src:155-158, 237-239)
DECLARE `The property lost or damaged` IS ONE OF
    `part of the item numbered`
        HAS `the item number` IS A NUMBER
            `the kind`        IS A `A kind of property`
    `surrounding property`
        HAS `on or near the site`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
            `owned by, or in the care, custody or control of, the principal or a contractor` IS A BOOLEAN
            `the kind`                                                              IS A `A kind of property`

-- The nature of the loss, in the words of the Part I insuring clause, exclusion 6 and
-- General Condition 5. `minor` ("hư hỏng nhỏ") is not defined (Finding 12).
-- (quoted at the rule that reads it: src:189)
DECLARE `The nature of a loss under Part I` HAS
    `sudden and unforeseen`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `physical loss or damage`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `repair or replacement necessary`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `discovered only when an inventory was taken` IS A BOOLEAN
    `repairable`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `minor`                                       IS A BOOLEAN

-- The money facts Article 2 and Article 3 turn on, and the consequential losses Part I
-- exclusion 2 removes. Each is a figure a loss adjuster or the Insured's accounts give.
-- * `the cost of restoring ...`: the cost necessary to put the item back in its condition
--   immediately before the occurrence; it does NOT include temporary repairs, alterations
--   or the Article 3 extra charges, which are separate fields.
-- * `the part of that cost of a kind not included in the sum insured`: Article 2 pays only
--   "to the extent that [the costs] are included in the sum insured" (fork F26).
-- * `the costs actually incurred by the Insured`: everything the Insured has actually spent
--   on the restoration or replacement, temporary repairs, extra charges and alterations
--   included. Article 2 pays only up to what was actually incurred, and never alterations.
-- (quoted at the rule that reads it: src:208-216, 227-231)
DECLARE `The costs of a loss under Part I` HAS
    `the cost of restoring the item to its condition immediately before the occurrence` IS A NUMBER
    `the part of that cost of a kind not included in the sum insured`                   IS A NUMBER
    `the actual value of the item immediately before the occurrence`                    IS A NUMBER
    `the salvage value`                                                                 IS A NUMBER
    `the costs actually incurred by the Insured`                                        IS A NUMBER
    `the cost of temporary repairs`                                                     IS A NUMBER
    `the temporary repairs form part of the permanent repairs`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the temporary repairs increase the cost of repair`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the cost of alterations, additions or improvements`                                IS A NUMBER
    `the extra charges for overtime, night work, work on public holidays and express freight` IS A NUMBER
    `the consequential losses claimed`                                                  IS A NUMBER

-- One loss under Part I.
-- * `the item had earlier been damaged and not repaired promptly and properly`: General
--   Condition 5 ends Bao Minh's liability for a damaged item that is not repaired promptly
--   and properly ("kịp thời chu đáo", not defined); this records that history (fork F12).
-- * `invoices showing the repair or replacement have been produced`: Article 2 pays only
--   after they are (src:218-220).
-- (quoted at the rule that reads it: src:119-120, 218-220)
DECLARE `A loss under Part I` HAS
    `the property`                                                          IS A `The property lost or damaged`
    `the nature`                                                            IS A `The nature of a loss under Part I`
    `the costs`                                                             IS A `The costs of a loss under Part I`
    `the item had earlier been damaged and not repaired promptly and properly` IS A BOOLEAN
    `invoices showing the repair or replacement have been produced`         IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `A liability under Part II`

-- One third party's claim against the Insured, arising from the occurrence.
-- * `the head`: Part II names two heads, (a) bodily injury or illness and (b) loss of or
--   damage to property; anything else is "a head the policy does not name".
-- * `accidental`: "bất ngờ" (sudden, unexpected); see GLOSSARY.md for the rendering.
-- * `the damages the Insured is legally liable to pay`: NOTHING until liability is
--   established; an established nil liability is JUST 0.
-- * `the item from which it arises`: the item named in Part I that the liability arises
--   from, if any; cover for a part that has been tested, operated or handed over ends
--   "and every liability arising from it" (src:47-51).
-- * the four exclusion facts are the words of Part II exclusions 2, 3(a), 3(b) and 3(d).
-- (quoted at the rule that reads it: src:247-256, 258-266, 274-291, 295-297)
DECLARE `A head of a third-party claim` IS ONE OF
    `bodily injury or illness, fatal or not`
    `loss of or damage to property`
    `a head the policy does not name`

DECLARE `A liability under Part II` HAS
    `the head`                                                        IS A `A head of a third-party claim`
    `accidental`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the damages the Insured is legally liable to pay`                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the claimant's costs of litigation recovered from the Insured`   IS A NUMBER
    `the costs and expenses incurred with Bao Minh's written consent` IS A NUMBER
    `the costs and expenses incurred without Bao Minh's written consent` IS A NUMBER
    `the item from which it arises`                                   IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `for doing, redoing, making good, repairing or replacing anything insured or insurable under Part I` IS A BOOLEAN
    `injury or illness of an employee or worker of the contractor, the principal or another firm connected with the works, or of a member of their families` IS A BOOLEAN
    `damage to property of, or in the care, custody or control of, the contractor, the principal, another firm connected with the works, or an employee or worker of any of them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `under an agreement of the Insured, and would not have attached without it` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `The dispute about a claim`

-- General Conditions 7 and 8.
-- * `liability admitted and the amount disputed`: General Condition 7 sends only a dispute
--   about the AMOUNT, "liability being otherwise admitted", to arbitration.
-- * `rejected`: the claim was rejected ("bị khước từ"), wholly or in part.
-- * the dates are NOTHING where the event has not happened.
-- (quoted at the rule that reads it: src:131-132, 143-146)
DECLARE `The dispute about the claim` HAS
    `liability admitted and the amount disputed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `rejected`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `date of the arbitral award`                 IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date proceedings were commenced`            IS A MAYBE DATE

§§ `A claim`

-- One claim: one occurrence, with its losses under Part I and its liabilities under Part II.
-- * `the date of assessment`: the date as at which the claim is assessed. The 14-day
--   notice bar and the three-month bar can only be judged once their time has run.
-- * `the date Bao Minh received notice`: NOTHING if no notice had been received by the date
--   of assessment. General Condition 5 counts RECEIPT, not dispatch (src:110).
-- * `the amount already paid under Part I for earlier occurrences`: what Bao Minh has paid
--   under Part I before, which the total sum insured under Part I caps in aggregate.
-- * `Bao Minh has paid under Part II condition 2`: Bao Minh has paid the limit (less sums
--   already paid) or a settlement sum for this occurrence, after which it is liable for
--   nothing more under Part II for it (src:310-314).
-- * the last two fields are General Condition 9. `Bao Minh's ratable proportion, as
--   determined` is NOTHING unless it has been agreed or determined; the document does not
--   say how it is computed (fork F20).
-- (quoted at the rule that reads it: src:109-111, 148-150)
DECLARE `A claim` HAS
    `the policy`                                                   IS A `The policy`
    `the conduct of the Insured`                                   IS A `The conduct of the Insured`
    `the occurrence`                                               IS AN `An occurrence`
    `the losses under Part I`                                      IS A LIST OF `A loss under Part I`
    `the cost of clearing debris from the site`                    IS A NUMBER
    `the liabilities under Part II`                                IS A LIST OF `A liability under Part II`
    `the date of assessment`                                       IS A DATE
    `the date Bao Minh received notice`                            IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the amount already paid under Part I for earlier occurrences` IS A NUMBER
    `Bao Minh has paid under Part II condition 2`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `other insurance covers the same loss or liability`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `Bao Minh's ratable proportion, as determined`                 IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the dispute`                                                  IS A `The dispute about the claim`

§§ `The vocabulary of the answers`

-- Not facts: the names of the answers the rules give. Each ground of non-liability names
-- the clause that supplies it, in document order.
DECLARE `A ground on which Bao Minh is not liable` IS ONE OF
    `preamble: the premium stated in the schedule has not been paid`
    `general exclusion (a): war, strikes, riot, confiscation and the other risks it lists`
    `general exclusion (b): nuclear reaction, radiation or radioactive contamination`
    `general exclusion (c): wilful act or wilful negligence of the Insured or its representative`
    `general exclusion (d): cessation of work, whole or partial`
    `period of insurance: the occurrence is outside it`
    `GC1: a duty of the Insured was not complied with`
        HAS `the duty` IS A `A duty of the Insured`
    `GC1: the questionnaire and proposal form were not answered truly and completely`
    `GC5: Bao Minh received no notice within 14 days of the occurrence`
    `GC5: liability for the item had ceased, because an earlier loss was not repaired promptly and properly`
    `GC8: all benefit is forfeited for fraud or a false declaration`
    `GC8: no proceedings were commenced within three months of the award`
    `Part I: the item is not named in the schedule`
    `Part I: not sudden and unforeseen physical loss or damage`
    `Part I: repair or replacement is not necessary`
    `Part I exclusion 3: faulty design, defective material or casting, or bad workmanship`
    `Part I exclusion 4: corrosion, wear, oxidation or scaling`
    `Part I exclusion 5: files, drawings, money, securities, packaging and the like`
    `Part I exclusion 6: discovered only when an inventory was taken`
    `Article 4: surrounding property not on or near the site, or not the principal's or a contractor's`
    `Article 4: not directly connected with the erection or testing of the insured items`
    `Article 4: construction or erection plant, machinery or equipment`
    `Article 4: the value of the surrounding property is not stated at Part I item 4 of the schedule`
    `Part II: not bodily injury, illness, or loss of or damage to property`
    `Part II: not accidental`
    `Part II: not directly connected with the construction, erection or testing of the insured items`
    `Part II: not on or near the site`
    `Part II exclusion 2: the cost of doing, redoing, making good, repairing or replacing what Part I covers`
    `Part II exclusion 3(a): injury or illness of employees or workers of the contractor, the principal or a connected firm`
    `Part II exclusion 3(b): property of the contractor, the principal, a connected firm or their employees`
    `Part II exclusion 3(c): a road vehicle, vessel, barge or aircraft`
    `Part II exclusion 3(d): a liability that exists only by the Insured's agreement`

-- Who bears the burden of proof under the clause that follows the general exclusions.
DECLARE `A burden of proof` IS ONE OF
    `on the Insured, to prove the loss or liability is covered`

-- The two readings of the questionnaire limb of General Condition 1 (fork F04). The rules
-- take reading (ii); the readings are named so that a test can run both.
DECLARE `A reading of the questionnaire limb of General Condition 1` IS ONE OF
    `reading (i): answering the questions is the condition`
    `reading (ii): true and complete answers are the condition`

§§ `The vocabulary of the regulative rules`

-- The acts the regulative rules speak of (bm-ear-duties.l4). An act that carries a field
-- is matched on it with PROVIDED.
DECLARE `An act under the policy` IS ONE OF
    `give notice of the occurrence`
    `inform the police of the theft`
    `notify Bao Minh of a material change, by telegram and in writing`
    `inspect the loss`
    `repair or replace the damaged item`
    `make or admit a material change that increases the risk`
        HAS `with Bao Minh's written approval` IS A BOOLEAN
    `make an admission, offer, promise, payment or indemnity`
        HAS `with Bao Minh's written consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appoint an arbitrator in writing`
    `pay the limit of indemnity less sums already paid, or a lesser sum for which the claims can be settled`
    `take over the defence or settlement of the claim`
